# Human-editable dependency input. To change deps: edit THIS file, then run
#   pip-compile requirements.in
# (pip-tools; use Python 3.11 to match the Docker image) to regenerate the
# locked requirements.txt, which is what the Dockerfile installs. Never edit
# requirements.txt by hand — it is generated.
# Every dep carries a `>=current,<next_major` ceiling. Deploys install the
# pip-compile lockfile (requirements.txt), so versions only move when someone
# re-runs pip-compile — the ceilings bound what a re-compile may pick (this is
# how `mcp` 2.0 took prod down on 2026-08-10 before it was pinned). Ceilings
# let patch/minor updates land on re-compile while blocking silent majors.
# Do NOT use exact `==` pins here — the lockfile owns exact pins.
