# NOT added, deliberately: numpy / scikit-learn. The initiative synthesizer
# (app/services/initiative_service.py) needs DBSCAN over cosine distance, which
# is a sklearn one-liner — but sklearn+numpy is ~100MB of image and tens of MB
# resident on a 512MB Fly machine that already runs a watchdog because it has
# been OOM-killed before. The algorithm is ~40 lines and exactly specified, so
# the service implements it directly and uses numpy for the distance matrix
# ONLY if it happens to be importable (both paths are asserted identical by
# tests/test_initiatives.py). Adding `numpy` here would buy the fast path for
# ~20MB if the corpus ever outgrows the pure loop; adding sklearn buys nothing
# the module doesn't already do.
